"Hobb, the south gate's night guard, takes a copper to leave a traveler out of the gate book."
"Marda Hesk has written three times to the Thornmere Guild hall for a holy mage; none has come."
"The town's grain store is half empty: the blight has kept woodcutters and hunters out since autumn."
"If the Wrenwood's blight breaks loose, Merrowgate's walls will hold beasts but not a blight tide."
